call_details.response:
The board is oriented with row 0 at the top. Columns 2, 3 and 4 are completely full, so the only legal moves are in columns 0, 1, 5 and 6.

No placement of an x produces four-in-a-row:
- column 0 lands at (2,0) and yields at most two consecutive x’s;
- column 1 lands at (1,1) and yields at most two consecutive x’s;
- column 5 lands at (2,5) and yields at most two consecutive x’s;
- column 6 lands at (5,6) and yields at most three consecutive x’s.

Player o, however, already has three consecutive pieces in row 2 (columns 2-4). The unique square that completes a horizontal four-in-a-row for o is (2,5), which is exactly where a disk dropped into column 5 would land. Consequently any move other than column 5 lets o win on the next turn.

The only move that prevents an immediate loss is therefore column 5.

Final Answer: 5

